🚀 Getting Started
Prerequisites

Node.js v18+
MongoDB (local or Atlas)
Cloudinary account

Installation
bash# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/AbuzarAli1122/Chat_App.git
cd Chat_App
bash# Install backend dependencies
cd server
npm install
bash# Install frontend dependencies
cd ../client
npm install
Environment Variables
Create a .env file in the /server directory:
envPORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_api_secret
Run the App
bash# Run backend (from /server)
npm run dev

# Run frontend (from /client)
npm run dev
Frontend runs on http://localhost:5173 | Backend on http://localhost:5000

📁 Project Structure
Chat_App/
├── client/                 # React frontend
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/     # UI components
│   │   ├── pages/          # Route pages
│   │   ├── store/          # Redux Toolkit slices
│   │   └── main.jsx
├── server/                 # Node.js backend
│   ├── routes/             # 3 REST API modules
│   ├── models/             # Mongoose schemas
│   ├── middleware/         # Auth middleware
│   ├── socket/             # Socket.IO logic
│   └── index.js
└── README.md

🔗 API Endpoints
MethodEndpointDescriptionPOST/api/auth/registerRegister new userPOST/api/auth/loginLogin & get JWTGET/api/roomsGet all chat roomsPOST/api/roomsCreate new roomGET/api/messages/:roomIdGet messages for a room

⚡ Socket Events
EventDirectionDescriptionjoin_roomClient → ServerJoin a chat roomsend_messageClient → ServerSend a messagereceive_messageServer → ClientReceive a new messageuser_onlineServer → ClientUser online status update
